{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"timeout 60 sed -n '1,240p' SYMBOLS.md && timeout 60 sed -n '1,260p' ERRORS.md && timeout 60 sed -n '1,300p' CONFIGS.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Dynamic symbol surface\n\nSource library: `../c_src/build/libdriver.so`\n\nCommand used:\n\n```text\nnm -D --defined-only ../c_src/build/libdriver.so\n```\n\nThe C shared object has exactly two globally defined dynamic symbols. Both are\nalso present with the exact same name in `target/release/libdriver.so`.\n\n| # | C symbol | C type | Rust symbol | Status |\n|---|----------|--------|-------------|--------|\n| 1 | `driver` | `T` | `driver` | [x] |\n| 2 | `fma_array` | `T` | `fma_array` | [x] |\n\nUndefined symbols in the C shared object are `memcpy` and `printf` plus normal\nweak ELF runtime symbols; these are libc/toolchain dependencies rather than\nlibrary API symbols.\n# Error surface\n\nMechanical inspection commands covered all C source and headers:\n\n```text\nrg -n \"RETURN_ERROR|return[[:space:]]+-1|return[[:space:]]+NULL|assert|if|switch|case|NULL|MIN|MAX|enum|[<>]=?\" ../c_src/include ../c_src/src\n```\n\nThe C implementation contains no explicit rejection, error return, assertion,\nnull check, range check, enum, or min/max constant. Therefore the source-derived\nexplicit rejection table has zero rows.\n\n## Generic FFI boundary cases\n\nThe task additionally requires generic boundary coverage even when the C source\ndoes not reject those inputs. The expected results below were measured in an\nisolated subprocess against the built C shared object. `driver` and `fma_array`\nreturn `void`, so normal completion/no mutation and process signal are the only\nobservable rejection outcomes.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | Tested |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|--------|\n| 1 | `driver` | `data == NULL`, `len == 0` | returns normally; writes no output | [ ] |\n| 2 | `driver` | `data == NULL`, `len == 1` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` | [ ] |\n| 3 | `driver` | non-null one-element `data`, `len == -1` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` | [ ] |\n| 4 | `driver` | non-null one-element `data`, `len == INT_MAX` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` | [ ] |\n| 5 | `fma_array` | all pointers `NULL`, `len == 0` | returns normally; no memory is accessed | [ ] |\n| 6 | `fma_array` | all pointers `NULL`, `len == -1` | returns normally; no memory is accessed | [ ] |\n| 7 | `fma_array` | `out == NULL`, other pointers valid, `len == 1` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` | [ ] |\n| 8 | `fma_array` | `mul1 == NULL`, other pointers valid, `len == 1` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` | [ ] |\n| 9 | `fma_array` | `mul2 == NULL`, other pointers valid, `len == 1` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` | [ ] |\n| 10 | `fma_array` | `add == NULL`, other pointers valid, `len == 1` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` | [ ] |\n| 11 | `fma_array` | all pointers reference one element, `len == INT_MAX` | process terminates with `SIGSEGV` | [ ] |\n\nThere are no public enums and no documented finite maximum length, so there is\nno enum-out-of-range case or documented-range-plus-one case beyond the\n`INT_MAX` oversized-length probes above.\n# Configuration surface\n\nThe public dynamic surface consists of the low-level `fma_array` entry point\nand the composed `driver` entry point. There are no runtime option flags,\ncompile-time Cargo features, enums, format selectors, element-type selectors,\nor byte-order modes.\n\nThe C branches only on each loop's `i < len` condition. Pointer aliasing is\nnevertheless part of the public low-level input shape because the parameters\nare not `restrict`-qualified, and shifted overlap changes later loop\niterations. Randomized positive-length rows cover lengths from 1 through 64.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `fma_array` | `len == 0`; all pointers may be null; empty/no-op shape | [ ] |\n| 2 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; four disjoint buffers; values constrained so multiply-add does not overflow | [ ] |\n| 3 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; four disjoint buffers; full-width `int` values including wrapping/edge cases | [ ] |\n| 4 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; `out == mul1`; `mul2` and `add` disjoint | [ ] |\n| 5 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; `out == mul2`; `mul1` and `add` disjoint | [ ] |\n| 6 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; `out == add`; `mul1` and `mul2` disjoint | [ ] |\n| 7 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; `out == mul1 == mul2`; `add` disjoint | [ ] |\n| 8 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; `out == mul1 == add`; `mul2` disjoint | [ ] |\n| 9 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; `out == mul2 == add`; `mul1` disjoint | [ ] |\n| 10 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; all four pointers exactly alias | [ ] |\n| 11 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; `mul1 == mul2`; `out` and `add` disjoint | [ ] |\n| 12 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; `mul1 == add`; `out` and `mul2` disjoint | [ ] |\n| 13 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; `mul2 == add`; `out` and `mul1` disjoint | [ ] |\n| 14 | `fma_array` | positive randomized length; `mul1 == mul2 == add`; `out` disjoint | [ ] |\n| 15 | `fma_array` | randomized length at least 2; `out` starts one element after a shared `mul1`/`mul2`/`add` buffer (forward shifted overlap) | [ ] |\n| 16 | `fma_array` | randomized length at least 2; shared `mul1`/`mul2`/`add` starts one element after `out` (backward shifted overlap) | [ ] |\n| 17 | `driver` | `len == 0`; null data; no output | [ ] |\n| 18 | `driver` | `len == 1`; randomized scalar values including `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, negative, zero, and positive | [ ] |\n| 19 | `driver` | randomized `len` from 2 through 64; randomized arrays including edge and multiply-add-overflow values; decimal newline output | [ ] |\n\n## Feature combinations\n\n`Cargo.toml` declares no features. The complete build matrix is therefore:\n\n| # | Cargo invocation mode | [ ] |\n|---|-----------------------|-----|\n| 1 | default features | [ ] |\n| 2 | `--no-default-features` (equivalent empty feature set) | [ ] |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
